#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078532 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2229bd-c425-5e53-b8cf-56f3f9f3f539" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Polynomial Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b95a64-4d37-5239-a5f8-32da2f360b0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "225a+15b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b95a64-4d37-5239-a5f8-32da2f360b0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "225a+15b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563055} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ecc700-8649-502f-87f9-0a514edc10b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3979b7c5-84a5-5fc8-9e6c-343a28511a49" :question/math-academy-id "q-167216" :question/problem "In terms of $a$ and $b,\\,p(15)=\\,${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=15$ into the expression for $p(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a{x}^{2}+bx \\\\ p(15) & =a(15)^{2}+b(15) \\\\  & =225a+15b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p(15)=225a+15b.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064348 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "075c23a4-9de9-59b5-bec4-575b0b0454f4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d436335e-8de5-5c08-ac68-22272df80bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270-15a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d436335e-8de5-5c08-ac68-22272df80bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270-15a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563410} :answer-field/id #uuid "187ca06a-34b2-52f2-bb4c-69c7613a1bfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "354145f6-5e93-540e-9ff9-3f90c1a259ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-167217" :question/problem "If the company produces fifteen wooden tables in a week, the weekly profit will be $\\$4\\,050.$ Find an expression for $b$ in terms of $a.$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that $p(15)=225a+15b.$ So, we need to solve the equation $225a+15b=4\\,050$ for the parameter $b.$\n\nWe need to isolate the variable $b.$ To do this, we treat $a$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $225a$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}225a+15b & =4\\,050 \\\\ 225a+15b-225a & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ 15b & =4\\,050-225a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15b & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ \\frac{15b}{15} & =\\frac{4\\,050-225a}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{15}b}{\\cancel{15}} & =\\frac{4\\,050}{15}-\\frac{225a}{15} \\\\ b & =270-15a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $b=270-15a.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283112f9-9ffe-5a11-bbfc-a5ba098b6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283112f9-9ffe-5a11-bbfc-a5ba098b6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563035} :answer-field/id #uuid "152e2f23-0e18-55aa-a6f1-c39bead952a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "967fdc49-d3aa-54f3-af09-6a561f202139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "967fdc49-d3aa-54f3-af09-6a561f202139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563279} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0751b7-37b1-5581-b463-69aae210a148" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b42bde79-43e7-5e0d-aa7f-ed2b4b36837d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167218" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $100a+15b=4\\,800.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}b=270-15a \\\\ 100a+15b=4\\,800\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=270-15a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100a+15b & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+15(270-15a) & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+4\\,050-225a & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a+4\\,050 & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a & =750 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=270-15a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =270-15(-6) \\\\ b & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=360.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e5366dd-a374-5abd-bdf6-77f378f97145" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bd929a1-7008-59ac-9b18-94c80aab8fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5184" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd929a1-7008-59ac-9b18-94c80aab8fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5184" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563260} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf53a58-c815-5351-a1ce-001a880e2d2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "527dba5f-2797-5f00-97de-509f725bd58d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167219" :question/problem "Determine the weekly profit if the company produces $24$ wooden tables in a week.\n\nThe company will earn$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$dollars." :question/worked-solution "From part 3, we have the function $p(x)=-6{x}^{2}+360x.$\n\nWe substitute $x=24$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(24) & =-6(24)^{2}+360(24) \\\\  & =-3\\,456+8\\,640 \\\\  & =5\\,184\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the company will earn $$5\\,184.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d1134c0-02ce-59c1-8238-4820da388f90" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Monomial From a Trinomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820e6076-fcaa-5c6f-b5f8-e29610fe3682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-20)(x-40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820e6076-fcaa-5c6f-b5f8-e29610fe3682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-20)(x-40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563233} :answer-field/id #uuid "56c69cd5-07d2-598b-b43c-0e186d6e3185" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "497dcd2a-064b-5508-ade6-dffd4f30752c" :question/math-academy-id "q-167220" :question/problem "The manager wants to determine the number of wooden tables the company should produce per week to make a weekly profit of $\\$4\\,800.$ The required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800=0.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be factored as $\\,$$6\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}} $)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We factor $6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800$ using the greatest common factor (GCF).\n\nComputing the GCF, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(6{x}^{2},360x,4\\,800)=6\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-360x+4\\,800 & = \\\\ 6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot ({x}^{2})+6\\cdot (-60x)+6\\cdot (800) & = \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-60x+800)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${x}^{2}-60x+800.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054658 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c9ba00d-9171-5732-8539-2e2943cce58e" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring Trinomials With Positive Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d6fadc-c6fc-54df-85f4-906ea6060968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d6fadc-c6fc-54df-85f4-906ea6060968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563231} :answer-field/id #uuid "69bddd2d-4ab6-5d13-b5cd-247cb058b864" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f01f8f3f-d44f-517a-a672-79bef06856d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-167221" :question/problem "Find the minimum number of wooden tables the company needs to produce per week to make a weekly profit of $\\$4\\,800.$\n\nThe company needs to produce$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ wooden tables per week." :question/worked-solution "From part 5, the required number of wooden tables $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n6\\cdot ({x}^{2}-60x+800)=0.\n$$\n\nDividing this equation by $6,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-60x+800=0.\n$$\n\nTo solve this equation, we want to find a factor pair of the constant term $(800)$ that also adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-60).$ The required factors are $(-20)$ and $(-40).$\n\nUsing this factor pair, we write the linear term as $-60x=-20x-40x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-60x+800 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-20x-40x+800 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-20x)+(-40x+800) & =0 \\\\ x(x-20)-40(x-20) & =0 \\\\ (x-20)(x-40)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solutions are $x=20$ or $x=40.$ Since we require the minimum solution, we conclude that the company needs to produce $20$ wooden tables per week to make a profit of $$4\\,800.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e1e439-ec4a-5577-80d5-3b113bf36e74" :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7608f3d-23f5-549b-a860-02910a5e6580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7608f3d-23f5-549b-a860-02910a5e6580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563417} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3549239-369c-5dc5-b97f-5b91a23e416d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f85c7e50-3cac-5133-ab86-e4e54ecc65fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-167222" :question/problem "The company wants to increase its output by implementing a new production model. The number of wooden tables ${a}_{n}$ produced in the $n$th week since the implementation of the new model is given by the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+4,\\,{a}_{1}=12,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nWhat is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence?\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=12,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+4 \\\\  & =12+4 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =16-12 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=12$ and $d=4$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =12+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =12+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=4n+8,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"}]}
